<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Hospital Data Entry Portal | LynxCom Sample</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/styles.css?v=hospital-ops-v2"></head><body><header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="../"><img src="../assets/lynxcom-logo.svg" alt="LynxCom Analytics"><span>Hospital Data Entry Portal</span></a><nav><a href="login.html">Role demo</a><a href="index.html">Dashboard</a><a href="portal.php">Portal</a><a href="../project-samples.php">Projects</a></nav></header><main class="shell"><section class="hero portalHero"><div><span class="eyebrow">Central Data Entry Portal</span><h1>Capture hospital operations from one structured form hub.</h1><p>Demo forms for patient registration, appointments, consultations, billing, lab, pharmacy, admissions and follow-up. Records are not submitted to a real hospital system.</p></div><aside class="heroCard"><b>Referential integrity demo</b><strong>Patient ID first</strong><p>In a production version, Patient ID connects appointments, consultations, invoices, pharmacy/lab and follow-up history.</p></aside></section><section class="portalTabs panel"><div class="tabButtons"><?php foreach($forms as $i=>$f): ?><button class="tabBtn <?=$i===0?'active':''?>" data-tab="tab<?=$i?>"><?=htmlspecialchars($f)?></button><?php endforeach; ?></div><?php foreach($forms as $i=>$f): ?><form class="portalForm <?=$i===0?'active':''?>" id="tab<?=$i?>"><h2><?=htmlspecialchars($f)?></h2><div class="formGrid"><label>Patient ID<select><option>PAT-2026-00001</option><option>PAT-2025-00422</option><option>New patient</option></select></label><label>Patient Name<input placeholder="Example: Aisha Mohammed"></label><label>Department<select><option>Cardiology</option><option>Obstetrics & Gynaecology</option><option>Paediatrics</option><option>Internal Medicine</option><option>Orthopaedics</option><option>General Surgery</option></select></label><label>Date<input type="date" value="2026-09-02"></label><label>Status<select><option>Completed</option><option>Pending</option><option>Scheduled</option><option>Cancelled</option><option>Requires follow-up</option></select></label><label>Amount / Value<input type="number" placeholder="0"></label><label class="wide">Notes<textarea placeholder="Capture important notes for dashboard reporting"></textarea></label></div><button type="button" class="btn primary" onclick="alert('Demo only: in production this would save to the hospital data source.')">Save demo record</button></form><?php endforeach; ?></section><section class="panel"><h2>What this portal demonstrates</h2><div class="trustList"><div><b>Cleaner records</b><span>Structured dropdowns reduce spelling errors and disconnected records.</span></div><div><b>Connected reporting</b><span>Every form can feed the owner, finance, doctor, lab and pharmacy dashboards.</span></div><div><b>Follow-up automation</b><span>Pending labs, missed appointments and unpaid invoices can create action queues.</span></div></div></section></main><footer class="footer">Fictional demo portal · No real patient data collected</footer><script>document.querySelectorAll('.tabBtn').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{document.querySelectorAll('.tabBtn,.portalForm').forEach(x=>x.classList.remove('active'));b.classList.add('active');document.getElementById(b.dataset.tab).classList.add('active')})</script></body></html>